<title>NORWAY: Statoil's NorFra gasline ahead of schedule.</title>
<headline>Statoil's NorFra gasline ahead of schedule.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Den norske stats oljeselskap AS (Statoil) said on Thursday the laying of the NorFra gas trunkline could be completed by August, one month ahead of schedule.</p>
<p>By Sunday, 445 km out of 840 km had been laid between the Draupner E riser platform in the Norwegian North Sea and the French port of Dunkerque.</p>
<p>The landfall in France, for what will be the world's longest submarine pipeline, is already completed.</p>
<p>The trunkline is in position in the Norwegian and Danish sectors of the North Sea and is now being laid over the German and Dutch continental shelves, Statoil's Status Weekly newsletter said.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
